# UJH V2

Before implementing or changing UJH V2, read and follow:
- docs/upwork/v2/ARCHITECTURE.md
- docs/upwork/v2/BEHAVIOR-BASELINE.md
- docs/upwork/v2/DATA-CONTRACTS.md
- docs/upwork/v2/STATE-MACHINE.md
- docs/upwork/v2/MIGRATION.md

These files are authoritative for V2.

Rules:
- Build V2 alongside V1. Do not modify, disable, or archive V1 unless explicitly instructed.
- Prefer purpose-built official actions, then specialized n8n nodes, then simple orchestration. Use HTTP or small Code nodes only when they are clearer/necessary.
- Use deterministic logic before AI. AI must not own workflow topology, persistence, scoring arithmetic, or authoritative state.
- Keep workflows small, single-purpose, and readable. Do not hide complexity in giant expressions.
- Reuse shared services for repeated config loading, job loading, event logging, and state transitions.
- Do not silently change architecture, schema, scoring semantics, protected Slack commands, state semantics, security/credentials, dependencies, paid services, or supported V1 behavior.
- Resolve ordinary implementation, wiring, expression, validation, retry, fixture, layout, and test failures autonomously.
- Implement, test, repair, retest, and report completion.
